6.1 Modularity
The LSX-64 design demonstrates strong modularity through its ISA extension framework:
* LSX-64I (base integer): 67 instructions
* LSX-64A (atomic): 8 instructions (LL/SC, AMO)
* LSX-64V (vector): 12 instructions (VADD.W, VMUL.W, etc.)
* LSX-64BT (binary translation): 6 instructions for x86/ARM translation
Each extension is independently simulatable and can be added or removed without modifying the core pipeline logic. The simulator's OpType enum and instruction format system allow new instructions to be added with minimal code changes.
